# TEMPORARY bring-up instrumentation. Delete this whole directory once the
# 4.9 port's boot hang is found -- see drivers/p49debug/p49-bootbeacon.c.
config P49_BOOTBEACON
	bool "4.9 port boot beacon (TEMPORARY, panics on purpose)"
	depends on DEBUG_KERNEL || !EXPERT
	help
	  TEMPORARY. This kernel has never booted and there is no console
	  available (no serial cable, CONFIG_VT off so no framebuffer console,
	  and the bootloader's "ecd_setup=disable" turns Samsung's ECD off after
	  CONFIG_CMDLINE is applied, so it cannot be overridden). A hang is
	  therefore completely invisible.

	  Enabling this makes the kernel panic deliberately at the end of
	  device probing, so that the pstore ramoops backend records the log up to
	  that point. Read it afterwards with:

	    adb pull /sys/fs/pstore/dmesg-ramoops-0

	  It is paired with turning CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE off, because with pmsg
	  writing continuously into the same buffer there is no room left for the
	  panic-time dmesg record -- which is why no dmesg-ramoops record has ever
	  appeared despite the kernel plainly dying.

	  If unsure, say N. This must not survive into a shipping kernel.

config P49_BOOTBEACON_MS
	int "Boot beacon delay in ms"
	depends on P49_BOOTBEACON
	default 10000
	help
	  How long after late_initcall the beacon waits before panicking. Raise it
	  to let more of boot complete before the panic; lower it toward 0 to
	  bisect an early hang. Moving the beacon's initcall level is a code
	  change; this only moves the deadline.
